{"id": "bce72253-d746-46bf-bf40-1c2baf0a7a42", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I need to find the actual Bedrock quota limit in us-east-1, which means checking Service Quotas rather than guessing. Since I don't have direct AWS access in my toolset, I'll need to delegate this lookup to a subagent that can query the account directly.

I'll first tell the user my plan, then dispatch a subagent to check applied vs default Service Quotas for Bedrock InvokeModel requests and token limits, cross-reference CloudWatch metrics like InvocationThrottles over the past week to see which models are actually hitting throttling, and check whether cross-region inference profiles are in play, keeping everything read-only and documentation-verified.

"}]}

{"id": "096df46e-6c72-4e44-a063-86b8ba30027a", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check your applied Bedrock quotas in us-east-1 against the defaults. I'll also look at which models are being throttled and when. Then I'll give you recommendations.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_xTIO4DaUNl08LKUKCv0sep", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-quota-check", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics", "verifying-with-docs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine the actual Amazon Bedrock runtime quotas in us-east-1 for this customer and which models are being throttled, then recommend what to do. Use read-only calls only.",
  "context": "Customer says they are throttled on Bedrock in us-east-1 during business hours and say they never requested a quota increase. They want to know their actual limit. Agent space account is 012345678901_1 (also check other associated AWS accounts via list_associations if Bedrock usage exists there). Region us-east-1.",
  "steps_to_cover": [
    "Service Quotas (service code 'bedrock', us-east-1): for the relevant on-demand quotas (requests per minute and tokens per minute for InvokeModel/Converse, and cross-region inference profile quotas where present), report both the APPLIED value and the AWS DEFAULT value per model, and whether any quota has an increase request history (list_requested_service_quota_change_history_by_quota). Note that new/low-usage accounts often get lower-than-default applied values.",
    "CloudWatch AWS/Bedrock metrics over the last 7 days (per ModelId): Invocations, InvocationThrottles, InputTokenCount, OutputTokenCount, InvocationClientErrors, at 1-minute granularity for peak business-hours windows. Identify which models throttle, peak requests/min and tokens/min vs the applied quota, and whether throttling is RPM-bound or TPM-bound (note output token burndown multipliers for models such as Claude, per AWS docs).",
    "Check whether callers use cross-region inference profiles (inference profile ids with us. prefix) vs direct model ids, and whether provisioned throughput exists (list_provisioned_model_throughputs).",
    "Use documentation lookup to confirm current guidance on Bedrock throttling mitigation (quota increase process, cross-region inference, retries with exponential backoff, burndown rates, provisioned throughput, batch inference)."
  ],
  "criteria": "Return concise findings: per throttled model -> applied quota, default quota, observed peak usage, throttle counts and time-of-day pattern; whether a quota increase was ever requested; ranked recommendations. Clearly distinguish verified facts from inference. If any call fails for permissions, say which."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check Bedrock quotas and throttling metrics in us-east-1"}], "created_at": null}

